WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.540
- [Narrator] One night in March, 2023

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.520
in the Central African Republic,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.230
security cameras captured a group

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.900
of men hurling Molotov
cocktails over the fence

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.620
of a brewing facility owned by
French multinational Castel,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.370
one of the largest beverage
conglomerates in the world.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.000
Western intelligence
agencies would later confirm

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.490
that The Wagner Group was
responsible for the attack

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.283
that destroyed a large portion
of the brewery's stock.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.660
The arson wasn't a
random act of vandalism.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.010
It was part of a larger war

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:35.163
for influence in Africa
between Russia and the West.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.220
In the Central African Republic,

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.510
beer matters to Wagner

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.730
because French brands
have a large presence

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:42.933
in their former colony.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.920
Since the 1990s,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.050
Castel has produced a beer called MOCAF

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.793
in the Central African Republic.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.450
The MOCAF Brewery has been
one of the largest employers

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.763
in the country's limited
industrial sector.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.040
One year prior to the arson attack,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.380
Wagner broke ground on a competing brewery

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.810
north of the capitol, Bangi.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.660
They've rapidly scaled up
production and distribution

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.150
of their own beer brand
called Africa Ti L'Or,

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.623
which is sold as Russian.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.520
Castel was able to keep
producing its MOCAF beer

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.680
throughout CAR's civil war,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.333
but not without controversy.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.710
In 2021, a report by the
investigative nonprofit group,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.120
The Century detailed

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.900
how Castel protected its
business interests in CAR

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.030
by making cash payments to rebel groups

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.553
like the Union for Peace or UPC.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.360
Castel did not respond
to requests for comment

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.193
but in the past,

00:01:40.193 --> 00:01:41.850
they've denied these
payments were criminal

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.563
and that they fueled the conflict.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.050
Using the details in the report,

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.480
Wagner saw an opportunity
to sell its narrative

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.830
about the role of the French

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:53.070
as exploitative colonizers in the country.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.690
In January, 2023,

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.720
a group of social media
accounts began simultaneously

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.707
spreading the same message,

00:01:59.707 --> 00:02:01.707
"Castel supports terrorism."

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.660
One meme spread by the campaign
depicted bottles of MOCAF

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.547
loaded into an assault
rifle with the message,

00:02:09.547 --> 00:02:13.137
"Each bottle purchased is a
bullet in the gun of bandits."

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.370
Disinformation experts the
journal spoke to confirmed

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.680
these accounts were connected to Wagner

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.690
and said the campaign bears the hallmarks

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:24.633
of one of Wagner's online
influence operations.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.440
Wagner's campaign also used offline means

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:29.760
of spreading this message

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.980
like billboards and flyers.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.530
One flyer read "With each Castel purchase,

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.927
you fund the war and kill yourself."

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.120
The group also organized demonstrations

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.520
where protestors poured
out bottles of MOCAF

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.973
while holding signs about
Castel's support for armed groups.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.450
The protests were amplified

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.633
by Wagner funded social media
accounts and news outlets.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.160
Wagner used its existing
network of businesses

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.520
to supply, build, and staff its brewery.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.250
Most Wagner businesses in CAR are centered

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.403
on natural resources like
gold, diamonds, and timber.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.880
Africa Ti L'Or represents a shift

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.003
for Wagner into businesses
that engage with the public.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.670
Selling Russian beer

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.100
to Central Africans
provides an opportunity

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.133
to sell a positive image for
Russia's role in the country.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.610
Many of the same accounts that took part

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:33.000
in the campaign against
Castel now tout Africa Ti L'Or

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:33.933
as an alternative.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.620
Representatives for
Wagner and Africa Ti L'Or

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.903
did not respond to requests for comment.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.600
Wagner's message about Castel
mirrors its broader message

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.640
that the French exploited the country

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.860
and contributed to its violence,

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:52.515
and that Russia and
Wagner are here to help.

00:03:52.515 --> 00:03:56.765
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:00.870
- [Narrator] Across Africa,

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.790
Wagner has organized demonstrations

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.350
and social media campaigns,

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:07.533
promoting Russia as an alternative
to France and the West.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.370
Since the attack, Castel has
continued to produce its beer

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.940
in CAR and Wagner's
future role in the country

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.460
appears to be in flux after
the death of its leader,

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.587
Yevgeni Prigozhin,

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.213
but their presence
remains deeply ingrained.

